      "writtenOn": "2021-02-13T02:10:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looking at this set of CLs it feels like a hodge-podge of changes.\n\nIf you want to focus on the cache, we should eliminate the email/adn changes.  Those changes will have their own set of comments, but blending it all into one makes this unmanagable.",
      "revId": "a4921b15d2bc2227660b06eaba1b289d839de54c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3652a731_ab1dd1bb",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002609
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-13T03:01:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we need to focus on simplifying.\n\nIf we focus on the RIL and the cache - the cache should just be an optimization, not adding any new features.  For example tracking and enforcing sim limits is a new feature that will alter behavior depending on whether this optional HAL is in use.\n\nThis carries through into the other CLs - we shouldn\u0027t have a separate and parallel set of functions.  Reading and writing of sim contacts is already supported and those API should use or not use your cache depending of availability, but all current users should get the benefit without having to switch API (and we shouldn\u0027t develop and support two sets of API).",
      "revId": "a4921b15d2bc2227660b06eaba1b289d839de54c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "073ca91b_84da7498",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/IccPhoneBookInterfaceManager.java",
